    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Saker appears to be a simple priest, but in truth he&apos;s a spy for the head of his faith. Wounded in the line of duty by a Lascar sailor&apos;s blade, the weapon seems to follow him home. Unable to discard it, nor the sense of responsibility it brings, Saker can only follow its lead. The dagger puts Saker on a journey to distant shores, on a path that will reveal terrible secrets about the empire, about the people he serves, and destroy the life he knows. The Lascar&apos;s dagger demands a price, and that price will be paid in blood.</marc:subfield>
